; AmiCode.cd - Katalogbeschreibung fuer AmiCode und AmiCodeIDE.
;
; Die hier stehenden Texte sind die EINGEBAUTEN, also Englisch. Sie greifen,
; wenn kein Katalog passt. Uebersetzungen stehen in catalogs/<sprache>.ct.
;
; Format je Eintrag:   MSG_NAME (id//)
;                      Der Text (eine Zeile, C-Escapes wie \n und \33 erlaubt)
; Ein _ markiert die Tastaturabkuerzung eines Knopfes.
; printf-Platzhalter (%s, %ld ...) muessen in jeder Uebersetzung in derselben
; Reihenfolge stehen - tools/locale.py prueft das.
; Nummern werden fortlaufend vergeben: neue Eintraege nur ans ENDE haengen,
; sonst zeigen alte Kataloge falsche Texte.
;
#version 0
MSG_CLI_ERROR (0//)
Error: %s\n
MSG_CLI_SWITCH_DIR (//)
Switch with: CD \"%s\"\n
MSG_CLI_ASK (//)
\n  ? %s\n    Allow? [y]es / [n]o / [a]lways / [q] abort task (Return = no): 
MSG_CLI_NO_INPUT (//)
(no input possible - refused)
MSG_CONTINUE_PROMPT (//)
Continue the interrupted work.
MSG_CLI_USAGE (//)
AmiCode %s - coding agent for AmigaOS\nUsage: amicode [MODE safe|project|full] [STEPS n] [RESUME] [<task>]\nWithout a task: interactive mode. Works in the current directory.\nCTRL-C aborts the running command or task.\n
MSG_CLI_INTERACTIVE (//)
Interactive mode. /help lists the commands, /exit quits.
MSG_CLI_PROMPT (//)
Task
MSG_CLI_NO_CONFIG (//)
Cannot read configuration '%s'.\n
MSG_CLI_BAD_MODE (//)
Unknown mode '%s' (safe, project, full)\n
MSG_CLI_NO_CWD (//)
Cannot determine the current directory
MSG_NETWORK_ERR (//)
Network: %s\n
MSG_CLI_BANNER (//)
AmiCode %s | %s: %s | mode %s | max. %d steps\nProject: %s\n
MSG_NO_MODEL (//)
(no model)
MSG_NO_MEMORY (//)
Out of memory
MSG_CLI_NO_SESSION (//)
No saved session found (%s).\n
MSG_CLI_RESUMED (//)
Session with %d messages resumed.\n
MSG_SESSION_ARCHIVE_FAIL (//)
Could not archive the session (%s)
MSG_SESSION_UNKNOWN (//)
No session \"%s\" - /sessions shows the list.
MSG_SESSION_CURRENT (//)
Current session: %s\n
MSG_SESSION_CURRENT_EMPTY (//)
Current session: (still empty)\n
MSG_SESSION_NONE_ARCHIVED (//)
No archived sessions.\n
MSG_SESSION_LIST_HINT (//)
Resume: /resume <no>, delete: /sessions delete <no>
MSG_SESSION_DELETE_FAIL (//)
Delete failed: %s
MSG_SESSION_DELETED (//)
Session %s deleted.
MSG_SESSION_DISABLED (//)
Sessions are not saved ([agent] session=none).
MSG_SESSION_LOAD_FAIL (//)
Could not load session %s.
MSG_SESSION_NOT_FOUND (//)
No saved session found.
MSG_SESSION_LOADED_CONT (//)
Session with %d messages loaded - just keep typing.
MSG_CTX_PRUNED_AUTO (//)
(Context trimmed: %d old tool results removed, now %ld KB)
MSG_RULES_LOADED (//)
Project rules loaded from %s.
MSG_CTX_TOO_SMALL (//)
The context of %ld tokens is too small: right after summarizing, %ld tokens are already used (system prompt, tools, working note). Please enter at least 8192 in the settings.
MSG_CTX_AUTO_COMPACT (//)
Context %ld%% full (%ld of %ld tokens) - summarizing the session and continuing.
MSG_OLLAMA_CTX (//)
Ollama works with only %ld tokens of context; the request (%ld tokens) gets cut and the model loses the beginning (system prompt, tools).
MSG_OLLAMA_CTX_FIX (//)
Fix: set OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=32768 on the Ollama machine and restart Ollama, or use /compact.
MSG_ABORTED_CTRLC (//)
Aborted (CTRL-C)
MSG_COST_LIMIT (//)
Cost limit reached: this task has already cost %s (limit $%s). Continue with \"go on\" or change the limit in the settings.
MSG_NO_MEMORY_CONV (//)
Out of memory for the conversation
MSG_STEP_THINKING (//)
[%d] thinking ...
MSG_TEXT_TOOLCALL (//)
(tool call recognized in the text)
MSG_SAME_ERROR (//)
(same error, %d times now)
MSG_TASK_ABORTED (//)
Task aborted by the user.
MSG_LOOP_STOPPED (//)
Stopped: the agent keeps repeating the same failing steps. Tip: describe the error in more detail, then continue - or choose another model.
MSG_STEP_LIMIT (//)
Step limit (%d) reached - task incomplete, can be continued.
MSG_DONE_COST (//)
, cost %s
MSG_DONE_CACHED (//)
(%d steps, tokens: %ld in, %ld of them cached / %ld out%s)
MSG_DONE (//)
(%d steps, tokens: %ld in / %ld out%s)
MSG_COMPACT_NOTHING (//)
Nothing to summarize.
MSG_COMPACT_RUNNING (//)
Summarizing the session ...
MSG_COMPACT_FAIL (//)
Summary failed: %s
MSG_EMPTY_ANSWER (//)
empty answer
MSG_COMPACT_DONE (//)
Session summarized: %ld KB -> %ld KB.
MSG_PRUNE_DONE (//)
%d old tool results removed: %ld KB -> %ld KB.
MSG_HELP (//)
/help           this overview\n/status         version, model, mode, project\n/context        size of the conversation\n/tokens         tokens used\n/model [name]   list available models or switch for this session\n/compact [focus] summarize the conversation and continue with that\n/prune          remove old tool results\n/diff           show the changes of this session\n/undo           restore the last changed file\n/reset          start a new session (the old one is archived)\n/sessions [delete <no>]  list or delete archived sessions\n/resume [no]    resume the last or an archived session\n/skills         knowledge skills and their mode (always/auto/off)\n/toolchains [scan] list installed compilers/interpreters or search again\n/new <tool> <directory>  create a new project, e.g. /new vbcc Work:Projects/demo\n!command        run a command yourself, the output goes to the model with the next task\n!!command       run a command yourself, the output is only for you\nFull manual: AmiCodeIDE.guide (in the IDE: HELP key or Amiga-H)
MSG_OUTPUT_TO_MODEL (//)
(The output goes to the model with the next task.)
